WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.404
Hi, I'm Gantry!

00:00:02.404 --> 00:00:07.604
IFM turned its K2 Horizon models into an Arabic family, without starting from scratch.

00:00:07.604 --> 00:00:08.719
Here is how.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.572
The new models add no Arabic tokens.

00:00:12.572 --> 00:00:16.739
The base vocabulary already held them, so adapting is just more training.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:22.837
The older adapted models had to add thirty-two thousand Arabic tokens to

00:00:22.837 --> 00:00:26.039
Llama two, and train their new embeddings alone first.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:30.174
This time the tokenizer is byte for byte the base's, every tensor

00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:32.651
keeps its shape, and only the values move.

00:00:34.342 --> 00:00:37.904
Start from the K2 Horizon weights near the end of their mid-training.

00:00:38.324 --> 00:00:41.956
Keep pre-training on Arabic, with a quarter of each batch replayed from

00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:44.377
the base's own data, so old skills stay.

00:00:44.797 --> 00:00:48.170
Then a short cool-down, fine-tuning, and an anti-repetition pass.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.451
The smallest model moved furthest, and its Arabic output rows moved about

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.704
twice as far as the English ones.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.614
Why no new tokens: an English-first tokenizer spends six tokens per Arabic word.

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:03.269
The base spends under one and a half.

00:01:04.925 --> 00:01:09.636
The speech model borrows Qwen's audio encoder, fine-tuned: about thirteen audio tokens

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.206
per second of sound.

00:01:11.626 --> 00:01:15.522
A small new projector feeds them to a decoder shaped exactly like

00:01:15.522 --> 00:01:17.469
the three point seven billion model.

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:22.027
It writes the transcript, names the dialect, and adds vowel marks on request.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.388
The most accurate open Arabic speech model?

00:01:25.388 --> 00:01:28.670
On six test sets, by about a third of a point,

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.863
in IFM's own run.

00:01:31.725 --> 00:01:36.303
If the base's vocabulary already covers the language, adapting it is just training.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.809
Same tokenizer, same shapes, new weights.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.100
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:45.700
I'm Gantry.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.001
Bye!
